/************************************************************************************* 

Program Name           : _003_kmplot_sidak_1.sas  

Path                   : sg1/_003_kmplot_sidak/

Purpose                : Kaplan-Meier Plot 

Input Datasets/Views   : Input data is generated by this program itself.

Macro calls external   : None

Production Outputs     : &Program..rtf  
                         &Program..pdf
                         &Program..sge
                         
Qualification Outputs  : &Program._qrt.sas7bdat     - Quartiles - Median and 95% CI 
                         &Program._tst.sas7bdat     - Log Rank Homgeneaity Test 
                         &Program._sg.sas7bdat      - Statistical Graphic output dataset
                         &Program_._srvdif.sas7bdat - Sidak Adjusted Multiple Pairwise Test
 
Program Flow           : 1) Set SAS options and style template libname
                         2) Set global macro variable  
                         3) Create the format 
                         4) Generate data
                         5) Run proc lifetest to get output datsets.     
                         6) Put subject count, median, median CIs, into treatement format.
                         7) Redefine format with big N and Median (95% CI) 
                         8) Put overall log-rank p-value into a macro variable.                               
                         9) Put pairwise sidak adjusted p-values into a macro variables.
                        10) Run proc lifetest to get SG output datset.                       
                        11) Post process SG output datsets.                                  
                             a) Offset error bars
                             b) Delete error bar if collapsed to a single line 
                             c) Offset censors
                        12) Block plot processing for "Subject at risk" 
                             a) sort by time
                             b) set missing character to blank                               
                        13) Set ODS graphics on and specify required ODS graphics 
                            parameters to create a PDF output 
                            for presentation.  
                        14) Define titles.    
                        15) Define the GTL program based on the SG dataset.                 
                        16) Run the GTL program.                                             
                        17) Close PDF output file and write to disk.                    
                        18) Set ODS graphics options for RTF file
                        19) Run the GTL program.                                             
                        20) Close RTF output file and write to disk.                    
                        21) Delete temporary PNG files.                         

Mod#    Ver#    Date            Username           Description
---     ----    -------         -----------        ---------------------------------------------------
001     1.00    5/11/26         dgianneschi        Create.
*********************************************************************************************/

